course: dictionary
lesson: 3565
title: Fertilisation in plants
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Fertilisation is when two special cells join together to start a new living thing. In a flower, pollen joins an egg cell, and this joining is what makes a seed possible. «After pollination, the pollen and the ovule join (fertilisation), the ovule becomes a seed, and the part around it grows into a fruit.»
explain: Look at the words around fertilisation to see the order. Pollination comes first, then fertilisation, then the ovule becomes a seed. «After fertilisation the ovules become seeds and the flower's ovary, the swollen bottom part of the pistil, grows into a fruit.» The word «after» is a clue that fertilisation comes before the seed and the fruit.
explain: Fertilisation has a second meaning too. Gardeners and farmers use it for putting fertiliser on soil to help plants grow. Check the sentence: if it is about flowers, pollen and seeds, it means joining cells. If it is about soil and crops, it means fertiliser.
fact: Fertilisation is when a male cell and a female cell join to start a new living thing.
fact: In plants, the order is pollination, then fertilisation, then seed formation, then seed dispersal, then germination.
fact: In animals, fertilisation happens when a sperm joins an egg.
fact: The American spelling is «fertilization».
fact: Fertilisation of soil means putting fertiliser on it to feed crops.
exercise: In a flower, what joins with the egg cell during fertilisation? | *Pollen | Water | Petals | Soil
exercise: «After fertilisation the ovules become seeds.» What do the ovules become? | Roots | Pollen | Fruit | *Seeds
exercise: A farmer says, «We did fertilisation on the field this morning.» What does she mean? | Picking the fruit from the trees | *Putting fertiliser on soil to help crops grow | Watering the crops at night | Two cells joining to start a new plant
test: Which step comes first in a plant's life cycle? | Germination | Seed formation | *Pollination | Seed dispersal
test: In animals, fertilisation happens when a sperm joins what? | A leaf | A root | A seed | *An egg
exam: «After pollination, the pollen and the ovule join (fertilisation), the ovule becomes a seed.» What does the ovule become after fertilisation? | A root | A fruit | A petal | *A seed
